 <flight_control name="FCS: myrocket">

  <property value="12.65">fcs/rail-travel-ft</property>
  <channel name="Rail">
   <fcs_function name="fcs/rail-margin-ft">
     <function>
       <difference>
         <difference>
           <property>position/h-agl-ft</property>
           <property>ic/h-agl-ft</property>
         </difference>
         <product>
           <property>fcs/rail-travel-ft</property>
           <sin><property>attitude/theta-rad</property></sin>
         </product>
       </difference>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>
   <switch name="fcs/off-rail">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="OR" value="1.0">
       fcs/rail-margin-ft gt 0.0
       simulation/sim-time-sec gt 2.0
     </test>
   </switch>
  </channel>

  <property value="10000.0">fcs/target-apogee-ft</property>

  <channel name="Airbrakes">

   <fcs_function name="fcs/coast-vt2">
     <description>Terminal-velocity squared for the coast, ft2/s2.
       vt2 = 2*W / (rho * S * Cd), built from live weight and density so the
       estimate adapts to mass and altitude without being told about them.

       Cd IS THE STOWED VALUE ON PURPOSE. The estimate therefore answers
       "where do I go if I stow the brake now", and the loop's job is to drive
       that quantity to the target: the moment it reaches the target, stowing
       the brake delivers the target, which is exactly when braking should
       stop.

       A version including the current brake position in Cd was tried and is
       much worse: nominal-day error went from +28 ft to +383 ft and peak
       deployment fell from 1.00 to 0.38. The mechanism is that proportional
       control needs a standing error to hold the brake out at all, since the
       command is kp times the error. With the brake in the estimate that
       standing error is a real apogee error, so the loop reads its own
       deployment as the problem being solved and retracts early. With the
       stowed form the standing error is measured against a prediction that is
       deliberately higher than the truth, and costs nothing.

       0.45 is the nominal stowed figure and is deliberately not adjusted to
       the true drag of the as-built airframe, which a flight computer would
       not know.</description>
     <function>
       <quotient>
         <product>
           <value> 2.0 </value>
           <property>inertia/weight-lbs</property>
         </product>
         <product>
           <property>atmosphere/rho-slugs_ft3</property>
           <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
           <value> 0.45 </value>
         </product>
       </quotient>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/coast-x">
     <description>v^2 / vt2, the argument of the log term.</description>
     <function>
       <quotient>
         <product>
           <property>velocities/h-dot-fps</property>
           <property>velocities/h-dot-fps</property>
         </product>
         <property>fcs/coast-vt2</property>
       </quotient>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/coast-ln">
     <description>ln(1+x) as a lookup rather than a natural-log operator, so
       the file does not depend on which maths elements a given JSBSim build
       exposes.</description>
     <function>
       <table>
         <independentVar lookup="row">fcs/coast-x</independentVar>
         <tableData>
                0.000    0.0000
                0.050    0.0488
                0.100    0.0953
                0.150    0.1398
                0.200    0.1823
                0.300    0.2624
                0.400    0.3365
                0.500    0.4055
                0.600    0.4700
                0.700    0.5306
                0.800    0.5878
                0.900    0.6419
                1.000    0.6931
                1.250    0.8109
                1.500    0.9163
                2.000    1.0986
                2.500    1.2528
                3.000    1.3863
                4.000    1.6094
                6.000    1.9459
         </tableData>
       </table>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/apogee-estimate-ft">
     <description>Closed-form apogee for a ballistic coast against quadratic
       drag at constant density:

           h_apogee = h + (vt2 / 2g) * ln(1 + v^2 / vt2)

       This replaces an energy estimate h + k*v^2/2g with a fixed k. A fixed
       factor cannot work: the share of kinetic energy lost to drag is not
       constant along the coast. With k = 0.75 the estimate runs about 535 ft
       high at burnout and about 615 ft low in mid-coast, changing sign in
       between. Mean absolute error over the coast falls from 314 ft to 20 ft
       with the form below.

       That error profile mattered because control authority is not spread
       evenly: holding the brake fully out for the first 4 s of coast gives
       most of the total authority (crosscheck.py authority gives the
       numbers). The estimator therefore has to be right early,
       which is exactly where the fixed-factor form was worst.

       Under +/-10% drag, +/-5% thrust and +/-5% mass, closed-loop apogee
       spread falls from 364 ft to 66 ft and worst-case error from 412 ft to
       35 ft. Open loop is 1480 ft.</description>
     <function>
       <sum>
         <property>position/h-agl-ft</property>
         <product>
           <quotient>
             <property>fcs/coast-vt2</property>
             <value> 64.348 </value>
           </quotient>
           <property>fcs/coast-ln</property>
         </product>
       </sum>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <fcs_function name="fcs/apogee-error-ft">
     <function>
       <difference>
         <property>fcs/apogee-estimate-ft</property>
         <property>fcs/target-apogee-ft</property>
       </difference>
     </function>
   </fcs_function>

   <pure_gain name="fcs/brake-cmd-raw">

     <input>fcs/apogee-error-ft</input>
     <gain> 0.001 </gain>
     <clipto>
       <min> 0.0 </min>
       <max> 1.0 </max>
     </clipto>
   </pure_gain>

   <switch name="fcs/brake-cmd-gated">
     <default value="0.0"/>
     <test logic="AND" value="fcs/brake-cmd-raw">
       propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs lt 1.0
       propulsion/engine[1]/thrust-lbs lt 1.0
       velocities/h-dot-fps gt 0.0
       position/h-agl-ft gt 1500.0
     </test>
   </switch>

   <kinematic name="fcs/airbrake-actuator">
     <input>fcs/brake-cmd-gated</input>
     <traverse>
       <setting>
         <position> 0.0 </position>
         <time>     0.0 </time>
       </setting>
       <setting>
         <position> 1.0 </position>
         <time>     0.5 </time>
       </setting>
     </traverse>
     <output>fcs/airbrake-pos-norm</output>
   </kinematic>

  </channel>

 </flight_control>

 <aerodynamics>

  <axis name="DRAG">

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_mach">
       <description>Axial drag coefficient vs Mach number</description>
       <product>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <table>
            <independentVar lookup="row">velocities/mach</independentVar>
            <tableData>
              0.00   0.45
              0.50   0.45
              0.80   0.48
              0.95   0.72
              1.05   0.78
              1.30   0.70
              2.00   0.58
              3.00   0.48
            </tableData>
          </table>
       </product>
    </function>

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_airbrake">
       <description>Air-brake drag increment. dCd = 2.0 at full deployment,
       referenced to body cross-section. Control authority (apogee lost if
       held fully deployed through the coast): crosscheck.py authority.</description>
       <product>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <property>fcs/airbrake-pos-norm</property>
          <value> 2.0 </value>
       </product>
    </function>

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_crossflow">
       <description>Crossflow drag (alpha), c = 25.29: c sin^2|sin| (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product>
            <value> 25.2937498613835 </value>
            <sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin>
            <abs><sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin></abs>
            <sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin>
          </product>
       </product>
    </function>

    <function name="aero/force/Drag_beta">
       <description>Crossflow drag (beta), c = 25.29: c sin^2|sin| (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product><value>25.2937498613835</value><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs><abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs></product>
       </product>
    </function>

  </axis>

  <axis name="LIFT">

    <function name="aero/force/Lift_alpha">
       <description>Normal force, Barrowman CN_alpha(Mach) x 0.5 sin(2 alpha); cluster fin set (v5).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <table>
            <independentVar lookup="row">velocities/mach</independentVar>
            <tableData>
              0.00   5.035
              0.30   5.053
              0.50   5.087
              0.60   5.111
              0.80   5.176
              0.90   5.176
              1.00   5.176
              1.20   5.176
            </tableData>
          </table>
          <product><value>0.5</value><sin><product><value>2</value><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></product></sin></product>
       </product>
    </function>

      <function name="aero/force/Lift_crossflow">
       <description>Crossflow normal force, lift component: c sin|sin| cos (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product>
            <value> 25.2937498613835 </value>
            <sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin>
            <abs><sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin></abs>
            <cos><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></cos>
          </product>
       </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <axis name="SIDE">

    <function name="aero/force/Side_beta">
       <description>Side force, same magnitude as the normal force.</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <table>
            <independentVar lookup="row">velocities/mach</independentVar>
            <tableData>
              0.00   5.035
              0.30   5.053
              0.50   5.087
              0.60   5.111
              0.80   5.176
              0.90   5.176
              1.00   5.176
              1.20   5.176
            </tableData>
          </table>
          <product><value>-0.5</value><sin><product><value>2</value><property>aero/beta-rad</property></product></sin></product>
       </product>
    </function>

      <function name="aero/force/Side_crossflow">
       <description>Crossflow side force: -c sin|sin| cos of beta (v6).</description>
       <product>
          <property>fcs/off-rail</property>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <product>
            <value> -25.2937498613835 </value>
            <sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin>
            <abs><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></abs>
            <cos><property>aero/beta-rad</property></cos>
          </product>
       </product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <axis name="PITCH">

    <function name="aero/moment/Pitch_damp">
       <description>Pitch damping due to pitch rate</description>
       <product>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <property>metrics/cbarw-ft</property>
          <property>aero/ci2vel</property>
          <property>velocities/q-aero-rad_sec</property>
          <value> -1278.2 </value>
       </product>
    </function>

      <function name="aero/moment/Pitch_crossflow_cp">
       <description>Exact body-axis reference-point couple for the cluster crossflow force family. Wind forces are transformed with the live alpha and beta; pitch = dx*Fz_body, yaw = -dx*Fy_body, where dx is the structural-coordinate force-centroid minus AERORP offset in ft.</description>
       <product><value>-0.71960000000000002</value><sum><product><value>-1</value><sum><property>aero/force/Drag_crossflow</property><property>aero/force/Drag_beta</property></sum><sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin><cos><property>aero/beta-rad</property></cos></product><product><value>-1</value><property>aero/force/Side_crossflow</property><sin><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></sin><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></product><product><value>-1</value><property>aero/force/Lift_crossflow</property><cos><property>aero/alpha-rad</property></cos></product></sum></product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <axis name="YAW">

    <function name="aero/moment/Yaw_damp">
       <description>Yaw damping due to yaw rate</description>
       <product>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
          <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
          <property>velocities/r-aero-rad_sec</property>
          <value> -1278.2 </value>
       </product>
    </function>

      <function name="aero/moment/Yaw_crossflow_cp">
       <description>Exact body-axis reference-point couple for the cluster crossflow force family. Wind forces are transformed with the live alpha and beta; pitch = dx*Fz_body, yaw = -dx*Fy_body, where dx is the structural-coordinate force-centroid minus AERORP offset in ft.</description>
       <product><value>0.71960000000000002</value><sum><product><value>-1</value><sum><property>aero/force/Drag_crossflow</property><property>aero/force/Drag_beta</property></sum><sin><property>aero/beta-rad</property></sin></product><product><property>aero/force/Side_crossflow</property><cos><property>aero/beta-rad</property></cos></product></sum></product>
    </function>
  </axis>

  <axis name="ROLL">

    <function name="aero/moment/Roll_damp">
       <description>Roll damping due to roll rate</description>
       <product>
          <property>aero/qbar-psf</property>
          <property>metrics/Sw-sqft</property>
          <property>metrics/bw-ft</property>
          <property>aero/bi2vel</property>
          <property>velocities/p-aero-rad_sec</property>
          <value> -0.8 </value>
       </product>
    </function>

  </axis>

 </aerodynamics>

 <output name="data_output/rocket.csv" type="CSV" rate="50">

  <property caption="Altitude AGL (ft)    "> position/h-agl-ft            </property>
  <property caption="Altitude ASL (ft)    "> position/h-sl-ft             </property>
  <property caption="Mach                 "> velocities/mach              </property>
  <property caption="Vertical speed (fps) "> velocities/h-dot-fps         </property>
  <property caption="True airspeed (fps)  "> velocities/vtrue-fps         </property>
  <property caption="Pitch angle (deg)    "> attitude/theta-deg           </property>
  <property caption="Alpha (deg)          "> aero/alpha-deg               </property>
  <property caption="Beta (deg)           "> aero/beta-deg                </property>
  <property caption="Pitch rate (rad/s)   "> velocities/q-rad_sec         </property>
  <property caption="Thrust (lbf)         "> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
  <property caption="Total mass (lb)      "> inertia/weight-lbs           </property>
  <property caption="CG x (in)            "> inertia/cg-x-in              </property>
  <property caption="Dynamic pressure(psf)"> aero/qbar-psf                </property>
  <property caption="Axial force (lbf)    "> forces/fbx-aero-lbs          </property>
  <property caption="Normal force (lbf)   "> forces/fbz-aero-lbs          </property>
  <property caption="Airbrake position    "> fcs/airbrake-pos-norm        </property>
  <property caption="Ground track (m)     "> position/distance-from-start-mag-mt </property>
  <property caption="Apogee estimate (ft) "> fcs/apogee-estimate-ft       </property>
  <property caption="vt2 (ft2/s2)         "> fcs/coast-vt2                </property>
  <property caption="Apogee error (ft)    "> fcs/apogee-error-ft          </property>
 </output>

 <external_reactions>
  <force name="rail-normal" frame="BODY" unit="LBS">
   <function>
     <product>
       <difference><value>1.0</value><property>fcs/off-rail</property></difference>
       <property>inertia/weight-lbs</property>
       <cos><property>attitude/theta-rad</property></cos>
     </product>
   </function>
   <location unit="IN"><x> 52.16 </x><y> 0.0 </y><z> 0.0 </z></location>
   <direction><x> 0.0 </x><y> 0.0 </y><z> -1.0 </z></direction>
  </force>
 </external_reactions>

</fdm_config>
